hondria. Selectively transports cytosine, guanosine, inosine and uridine (deoxy)nucleoside mono-, di-, and triphosphates by antiport mechanism. Catalyzes uniport at much lower rate (PubMed:25320081). May import (deoxy)nucleoside triphosphates in exchange for intramitochondrial (deoxy)nucleoside mono- and diphosphates, thus providing precursors necessary for de novo synthesis of mitochondrial DNA and RNA while exporting products of their catabolism (PubMed:25320081). Participates in mitochondrial genome maintenance, regulation of mitochondrial membrane potential and mitochondrial respiration."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}